I accept the other side of Tim's bet.

While I agree that Tim's idea is better than providing
the new list software free and selling "agents", I still think it will 
fall short of these revenue goals.  I'll be happy to go into
detailed critique in private, no need to be a stick-in-the-mud
in public.  Suffice it to say that I suspect I am part of 
the "silent majority" in seeing more trouble than worth from
the user's standpoint, especially when my dwindling savings account
enters the picture.  Thus, I will take up Tim May on his 
bet, putting up $10 that if his scheme is adopted, within one year the 
